# Mascot — Visual Design Brief

How the series mascot *looks*. Appearance only.

---

## Decided traits
These apply to every variant below.

- **Cute & cartoonish** — but not childish; must carry adult tone/language and deadpan delivery.
- **Simple** — few elements, easy to redraw and animate.
- **Hand-doll / puppet** base form (puppet cues: big expressive mouth, simple body, "held" posture).
- **Flat vector** render — crisp lines, flat color fills, no felt/fabric texture.
- **Reads at thumbnail size** — silhouette must survive as a small black blob.
- **Works on light + dark backgrounds.**

---

## Variants
Same decided traits, three fully-specced takes. React, tweak, or reject.

### Variant A — "Bit" · abstract blob-monster
- **Form:** rounded bean/egg body, no neck, two small side nubs for arms. One big horizontal puppet mouth splits the lower third.
- **Silhouette / proportions:** ~60% head-blob, 40% body — chunky, bottom-heavy, sits low. Side fuzz tuft (2–3 vector spikes) breaks the plain oval.
- **Color:** warm coral/tangerine body · off-white mouth interior · single dark accent for eyes · optional cream belly patch.
- **Eyes:** two plain black dots, small, set high and close — tiny eyes over a huge mouth = deadpan engine.
- **Mouth:** oversized lower-jaw puppet mouth, off-white/pink interior; range from thin closed line to wide gape.
- **Line/shading:** medium uniform outline, one flat shadow tone max.
- **Signature detail:** the fuzz tuft + oversized mouth combo.
- **Poses to support:** neutral host, wide-mouth talk, deadpan side-eye, surprised gape, small nub gesture.
- **Why it works:** zero real-world baggage, cleanest thumbnail blob, most "original IP."
- **Risk:** generic if tuft/color aren't distinctive enough.
- **Image prompt:**
  > Flat vector mascot character, cute cartoon hand-puppet monster. A chunky rounded bean-shaped body in warm coral-orange, bottom-heavy, no neck, with two tiny side nubs for arms and a small tuft of 2–3 spiky fuzz on top. Big horizontal puppet mouth splitting the lower third of the face, off-white interior. Two small black dot eyes set high and close together, giving a deadpan, dry-humored expression. Simple flat color fills, crisp medium-weight outlines, one soft flat shadow, no gradients, no texture. Friendly but not childish, capable of adult deadpan delivery. Centered front view, plain neutral light-grey background, clean negative space, strong readable silhouette. Character mascot design, sticker style, high contrast.

### Variant B — "Fox" · recognizable animal
- **Candidate animal:** fox (clever/curious, sharp silhouette). Other animals under consideration listed at bottom.
- **Form:** triangular ears carry recognizability. Head + small held body, big puppet mouth under the snout.
- **Silhouette / proportions:** big head, ears ~⅓ of total height, compact body. Pointed snout adds a directional read.
- **Color:** muted rust/terracotta (not neon) · cream muzzle + belly · dark ear tips + dark nose accent.
- **Eyes:** almond/leaf-shaped, slightly angled — reads sly without effort; black with tiny highlight.
- **Mouth:** puppet mouth opens under the snout; snout tip stays fixed so it still reads "fox" when open.
- **Line/shading:** medium outline, flat two-tone (body + belly), dark tips as third value.
- **Signature detail:** the two triangle ears — readable even as a black blob.
- **Poses to support:** neutral host, talking, ears-perked curious, ears-flat skeptical, sly grin.
- **Why it works:** instant relatability, strongest small-size silhouette.
- **Risk:** "clever fox mascot" is well-trodden; needs a twist.
- **Image prompt:**
  > Flat vector mascot character, cute cartoon fox hand-puppet. Big head with two large pointed triangular ears (dark tips) making up about a third of the height, compact held body, pointed snout. Muted rust-terracotta fur with a cream muzzle and belly, small dark nose. Almond-shaped, slightly angled black eyes with tiny highlights, giving a clever, sly-but-friendly look. Big puppet mouth opening beneath the snout. Simple flat two-to-three tone color fills, crisp medium-weight outlines, no gradients, no texture. Cute and approachable yet able to deliver dry adult humor. Centered front view, plain neutral light-grey background, clean negative space, strong readable silhouette. Character mascot design, sticker style, high contrast.

### Variant C — "Sock" · classic sock hand-puppet
- **Form:** a genuine tube-sock puppet worn on a hand. The mouth is the fold where the hand opens at the toe end; heel forms the back of the head. Stuck-on googly eyes on top, optional felt tongue.
- **Silhouette / proportions:** distinctive bent-tube / L-shape — sock bends at the "wrist," toe end juts forward as the snout/lower jaw. The bend is the recognizability, not a head-and-body split.
- **Color:** off-white / cream sock body · a couple of classic stripes at the cuff (red or navy) · pink/red felt mouth interior + tongue · white googly eyes with black pupils.
- **Eyes:** big round stuck-on googly eyes (white with black dot pupils), sitting slightly wonky on top — the wobbly handmade look is the charm.
- **Mouth:** the sock fold itself is the mouth; pink/red interior, small tongue; opens wide for talking, pinches to a line when deadpan.
- **Line/shading:** medium outline, flat fills; suggest the sock via a ribbed-cuff band and a heel seam line only — NO knit/fabric texture or gradients (keeps the decided flat-vector rule).
- **Signature detail:** googly eyes + striped cuff + the bent-sock silhouette — instantly "sock puppet."
- **Poses to support:** neutral host, wide-open talk, deadpan pinched mouth, curious tilt, tongue-out cheeky.
- **Why it works:** makes the hand-doll concept literal; honest/DIY warmth, handmade charm, feels personal (good for the personal-brand goal) and dodges any "mechanism" implication.
- **Risk:** can read lo-fi or childish if too plain — the deadpan expression + clean vector styling are what keep it adult.
- **Image prompt:**
  > Flat vector mascot character, cute classic sock hand-puppet. An off-white tube sock worn on a hand, bent into an L-shape so the toe end juts forward as a snout-like lower jaw and the heel forms the back of the head. A couple of simple red stripes around a ribbed cuff band, and a faint heel seam line. Big round stuck-on googly eyes (white with black dot pupils) sitting slightly wonky on top, giving a charming handmade look. The sock fold forms a wide puppet mouth with a pink-red interior and a small tongue. Simple flat color fills, crisp medium-weight outlines, no gradients, no knit or fabric texture. Cute and homemade yet able to deliver dry adult deadpan humor. Centered side-on view showing the classic sock-puppet profile, plain neutral light-grey background, clean negative space, strong readable silhouette. Character mascot design, sticker style, high contrast.

