## Animal alternatives (for Variant B)
Fox is the current pick. Fallbacks if fox feels too stock:
- **Axolotl** — frilly external gills = unique silhouette, inherently cute, almost no mascot competition. Playful/friendly read.
- **Fennec fox** — oversized ears carry the thumbnail read; cuter and less stock than a regular fox. Curious energy.
- **Bat** — big ears + wing shape, strong silhouette, nocturnal/curious; needs cute-ifying so it doesn't read spooky.
- **Octopus** — expressive, "many hands helping," great for gesture poses; busy silhouette + tentacles = more animation work.
- **Raven** — clever connotation, sharp beak silhouette; can read dark/ominous, needs softening to stay cute.
- **Parrot** — mimics/repeats speech (sly nod to how LLMs echo language), colorful, beak = strong read; risk of being too on-the-nose.
